Section 32.
The Governor shall vacate office upon:
death;resignation;
removal by the Board;
being an incompetent or quasi-incompetent person;
being absent from more than three consecutive Board meetings
without justification;
lacking any qualification or being under any prohibition under
section 30 or section 31.
The resolution of the Board removing the Governor under (3) shall
require votes of not less than three-fourths of the total number
of Directorsexcluding the Governor and the approval of the Council of Ministers.

